          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "لعل — laʿalla — \"it may be that; perhaps\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "لعل الطقس يتحسن غدا. laʿalla aṭ-ṭaqs yataḥassanu ghadan. Perhaps the weather will improve tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Like إن, it is followed by a noun or a pronoun: لعله, perhaps he."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "لعل (laʿalla) is an old native Arabic particle of hope or expectation, perhaps. Grammarians often trace it to ʿalla with la-; its origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
